# JukePI server settings. Copy this file to deploy/music-server.env (git ignores it), edit it, then run
#   PI=pi@raspberrypi.local ./deploy/deploy.sh
# deploy.sh installs it on the Pi as /etc/music-server/music-server.env (owner root, mode 600, readable by the
# service only). Format: KEY=value, one per line, no quotes. Anything here overrides the systemd unit.
# NEVER commit the real file: it will hold your Last.fm secret.

# --- Required: the address of THIS Pi as the amplifier sees it (fixed IP or DHCP reservation, never a .local name)
MUSIC_PUBLIC_URL=http://192.168.1.50:8765

# --- Where the music is (default /mnt/music/music)
#MUSIC_ROOT=/mnt/music/music

# --- The amplifier, if automatic discovery (SSDP) does not find it
#HEOS_HOST=192.168.1.60

# --- Last.fm (all optional; nothing is sent to Last.fm without LASTFM_API_KEY)
# Create an application at https://www.last.fm/api/account/create : it gives an API key and a "shared secret".
# The key alone enables "more like this" (the artist and title of the track being played are sent to Last.fm).
#LASTFM_API_KEY=
# The secret also enables scrobbling (what the amplifier plays is sent to your account). After the deployment,
# link your account once with: MUSIC_SERVER=192.168.1.50:8765 ./scripts/lastfm-link.sh
#LASTFM_SECRET=
# Account whose listening history lifts the suggestions when no account is linked (public profiles only)
#LASTFM_USER=

# --- Online cover lookup (sends artist and album names to MusicBrainz): off by default
#COVERS_ONLINE=1
#MUSICBRAINZ_CONTACT=you@example.org
